Hannah didn’t want to think anymore. Not when Laura was stretched out on the bed next to her, hair in a towel and wrapped in Hannah’s robe; her lips still slightly swollen from kissing.
‘You could stay… If you want?’ Hannah murmurs, pressing her lips against the back of her neck. Laura smelled warm, the lingering scent of Hannah’s shampoo too.
‘I have too much shit to sort out before work tomorrow. Not all of us have the luxury of being off.’ Laura teased gently.
‘I only have three more weeks off… fuck,’ Hannah groaned, flopping back on the bed. ‘I’ve gotten used to being able to lie in… and actually watch TV shows when they come out and not have it spoiled for me on Instagram.’
‘Enjoy it while it lasts. Don’t think you’ll get much time come February.’ Laura had a silly grin on her face.
‘It feels real now… I’m scared.’ Hannah admits. The girls start school in Moderna next week, and Hannah had so little time to get the house in order before her first day at Ferrari she’s convinced the stress is starting to make her hair fall out.
