‘I know–’
‘Can you blame me for wanting you close?’ Hannah murmured. Pressing a kiss against her hand. ‘We wouldn’t have to sneak around quite so much… This could be real… If you want.’
Laura could feel her stomach drop; the conversation she knew was coming had seemingly arrived. She didn’t feel brave enough to break both of their hearts on a cold January evening. Especially as Hannah was looking out nervously across a bright new horizon.
‘Of course I want to–’
