Laura checked around the room for anything she might have left. Hoping she could have forgotten something, an excuse to come back if she couldn’t bear what she’d done. There was nothing. Hannah walked with her to the door, still sniffling as Laura pulled her boots on. She drew out, wrapping her scarf around her, slowly buttoning her coat until she had no more time left to draw.
