‘I love you too.’ Laura smiled, tears still rolling down her cheeks. She pulled Hannah tight against her. Their lips met; she could barely taste Hannah through the salt of their tears, but it was enough. The kiss devolves to clinging desperately to the other, unwilling to be the first to break away. Hannah breaks first, her hand cradling Laura’s face, taking a final loving look at her features.
‘I really do love you,’ Laura whispered.
‘I know.’ Hannah sniffed.
‘I almost forgot,’ Laura croaked, her hand going to the silver band Hannah had placed on her finger last year. A promise that they’d see each other again. 
