Laura stepped into the dark hallway, Hannah in the doorway, illuminated by the hallway light behind her. Almost an angel.
‘Night.’
‘Drive safe.’
Laura nodded, every muscle in her body willing her back into Hannah’s arms as she turned away, down the dark stairs and into the night. Hannah’s sobbing got quieter and quieter until she left the foyer of her building and into the cold air.




